-| D-145 | 2026-11-13 | [was D-102 on an unmerged branch, merged to main 2026-11-14 (owner)] Product name **Rail8** (short form R8) replaces the working name Flottila (owner's decision, amends D-005). Logo, r8 mark and favicon set in `docs/brand/` (commit 88b7200): the accent-coloured `r` runs down into a rail under `ail` that ends in the 8; letters are outlines of Red Hat Display Bold (SIL OFL), colours are the PatternFly 6 brand tokens (`#0066cc`, `#92c5f9` on dark, `#151515` text). Nothing is renamed yet: repository, Maven groupId `io.flottila`, artifactIds, packages, env keys (`FLOTTILA_*`), the `flottila` CLI and the documents keep the old name until a rename row exists in BACKLOG. Domains `rail8.ai`, `rail8.io`, `rail8.dev`, `rail8.app` were unregistered on 2026-11-13 (registry RDAP), `rail8.com` is taken; none is registered by us yet. No trademark search was done. | Owner's criteria: short, easy to remember, international, a double meaning, a number as in WSO2, no ship motif. Associations that decided it: a rail is speed, direction and reliability, and "guardrails" ties it to AI; R8 reads as a numeronym like K8s; "rail-eight" sounds like "relate" and R8 like "rate"; 8 is strength in numerology, prosperity in China, the eight auspicious symbols of Tibet (one is the endless knot, everything connected) and infinity on its side; the letters R-A-I-L sum to 22, the numerologists' "master builder"; in the logo `ail` between `r` and `8` reads as "ai 1", AI first. Rail2 was the earlier favourite and was dropped because it reads as "the second track". Known collisions, accepted: Audi R8 (other trade class), Google's R8 Android shrinker, Ruby on Rails. Runners-up: Span2, Kept2, Spoy. |
